<title>GERMANY: SWIMMING-PANKRATOV BREAKS WORLD RECORD FOR MEN'S 200 BUTTERFLY.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-PANKRATOV BREAKS WORLD RECORD FOR MEN'S 200 BUTTERFLY.</headline>
<dateline>GELSENKIRCHEN, Germany 1997-02-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian Denis Pankratov set a world record for the short-course men's 200 metres butterfly when he clocked one minute 52.64 seconds at a World Cup swimming meeting on Saturday.</p>
<p>The previous best of 1:53.05 was set by Frenchman Franc Esposito in Paris in February 1994.</p>
